INT. WAREHOUSE ROLLER DERBY RINK - NIGHT

A banked track marked in tape. Folding chairs, a beer cooler, a hand-lettered scoreboard. A hundred spectators in leather and sequins roar.

Three skaters. One jam left.

BRONWYN "BRUTAL BRON" SANTOS-WEBB, thirties, jammer, star on her helmet. Fast. Bleeding from the lip.

MONIQUE "MAYHEM MO" OYELOWO, forties, blocker. Wide as a door.

RENATA "RAZOR" VASQUEZ, twenties, blocker. Small. Dangerous.

Whistle.

Bron charges. Mo steps in. Razor sweeps low. Bron hops, spins, and slams into Mo's shoulder. Razor's elbow takes her in the ribs. All three go down in a clattering heap, helmets cracking, wheels spinning in the air.

The crowd shrieks.

BRON
(from the floor)
Is she okay?

MO
I'm fine!

RAZOR
Not her. Her.

She points. Bron sits up. She is clutching her wrist.

Mo and Razor look at each other. They roll away at the same moment, and she gets up first, holding a hand down to Bron.

MO
Time out.

The crowd chants. Bron laughs through the pain, takes the hand, and lets herself be hauled up. Razor, grinning, high-fives her with the good one.
